===Etymology===
From New Latin {{m|la|anabaptista}}, from the Ancient Greek {{m|grc|ἀναβαπτισμός}}, itself from {{m|grc|ἀνά-||re-}} and {{m|grc|βαπτισμός||baptism}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A member of a [[radical]] [[wing]] of [[Christian]]s during the [[Protestant]] [[Reformation]] (such as a [[Mennonite]], an [[Amish]] person, a [[Hutterite]], a [[Brethren]] community, etc.).
# A member of any of several [[present-day]] [[church]]es.

